+Weight-only quantization of the text projections uses a fitted codebook instead of a uniform
+grid: the weight is normalized by a per-group scale, a global ``2**bits``-level codebook is
+fitted to the normalized weights with Lloyd iterations, and the per-group scale is then
+refined by least squares against the fitted levels.  For the same number of bytes this is
+measurably closer to the weight than a uniform quantizer (80-frame action error 0.153 vs the
+parent's 0.280 at identical sizes).  The forward dequantizes one output-row chunk at a time,
+so the transient bf16 weight never exceeds a few MB.
